{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Naming Convention.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Naming Convention.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender operator naming convention blender operator naming convention","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Naming Convention.md","fileName":"Blender Operator Naming Convention.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Operator Naming Convention","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Operator and Event System]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender Operator Type Registry","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Naming Convention.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Naming Convention.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender operator naming convention blender operator naming convention","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Naming Convention.md","fileName":"Blender Operator Naming Convention.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Operator Naming Convention","heading":"Blender Operator Naming Convention","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A core Blender operator identifier begins with its owning window-manager or editor prefix, continues with `OT`, and ends with the action name. Examples use prefixes such as `WM`, `CONSOLE`, and `OUTLINER`, allowing the identifier to reveal both scope and purpose.\n\nThe registration function commonly uses the same name as the identifier assigned to its [[Blender Operator Type Structure]]. That string becomes the lookup key in the [[Blender Operator Type Registry]] and connects event handling, UI binding, and Python invocation to one operation definition.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender Operator Type Registry","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Naming Convention.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Naming Convention.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender operator naming convention blender operator naming convention","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Naming Convention.md","fileName":"Blender Operator Naming Convention.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Operator Naming Convention","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[coreblenderdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender Operator Type Registry","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}